<title>GERMANY: German engineering job cuts seen slowing in 1997.</title>
<headline>German engineering job cuts seen slowing in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>LEIPZIG, Germany 1997-01-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's engineering industry will continue to shed jobs in 1997, albeit at a slower pace than in 1996, when it axed 120,000 to 140,000 jobs, the head of the engineering employers' federation Gesamtmetall said.</p>
<p>Werner Stumpfe said in a newspaper interview he would be happy if the cuts could be reduced to a third of last year's level.</p>
<p>A summary of the interview, to be published in Monday's edition of Leipziger Volkszeitung newspaper, was released on Sunday.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
